BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-211943@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261208T173000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261208T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261208T190000
SUMMARY:'Quin Chat & Screening: "MANGOK" 
LOCATION:The Muse
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 6 spots left
 \nStatus: Available\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/21
 1943\n\n5:30PM Reception\, 6:00PM Screening\, 6:25PM Discussion\nTwo days 
 before World Human Rights Day\, join us for a moving ’Quin Chat with Man
 gok Bol\, filmmaker Joshua Bennett\, and RefugePoint founder Sasha Chanoff
 \, exploring the extraordinary story behind Bennett’s documentary\, MANG
 OK. A South Sudanese “Lost Boy” who made Boston his home\, Mangok spen
 t more than a decade searching for family members separated by war. After 
 learning that his brother and sister-in-law had been killed and their four
  children were missing\, he embarked on a determined search with the suppo
 rt of Chanoff and RefugePoint. Three of his nieces and nephews have since 
 been welcomed to Boston\, while the search for the fourth continues in Sou
 th Sudan.\n\nThrough a conversation about perseverance\, family reunificat
 ion\, and the profound impact of community\, our guests will reflect on th
 e personal journey at the heart of the film and the broader challenges fac
 ing displaced families around the world. Together\, we will explore what i
 t means to rebuild a life\, the bonds that endure across borders\, and how
  one person’s refusal to give up can inspire a community to open its doo
 rs and its heart.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members
  only. Complimentary light bites and refreshments will be served. Cancella
 tions made within 24 hours of the event\, or failure to attend\, will resu
 lt in a $25 charge.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/211943
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-213342@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261208T190000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261208T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261208T203000
SUMMARY:Author's Circle Book Club: "All That Life Can Afford" with Emily Ev
 erett 
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 46 spots left\nS
 tatus: Available\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/21334
 2\n\nBookmark the date for an engaging conversation with Emily Everett\, a
 uthor of All That Life Can Afford\, a debut novel exploring ambition\, rei
 nvention and the price of belonging.\n\nFor Anna\, a young American raised
  on Austen novels and dreams of London\, life abroad was supposed to be a 
 fresh start. Instead\, she finds herself struggling to make ends meet—un
 til a tutoring job with the wealthy Wilder family takes her to Saint-Trope
 z. Drawn into an alluring circle of privilege\, parties and romantic possi
 bilities\, Anna discovers that the life she has imagined may demand more o
 f her than she anticipated. \n\nEqual parts glittering escape and thoughtf
 ul exploration of class and identity\, All That Life Can Afford asks how f
 ar we will go to become someone new—and what we risk leaving behind. Joi
 n us for a conversation about the pull of possibility\, the complications 
 of love and finding your place without losing yourself.\n\n*This event is 
 complimentary and reserved for members\, plus one registered guest. Compli
 mentary light bites and refreshments will be served. We kindly ask that al
 l cancellations be made at least 24 hours prior to the start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/213342
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
